{"id":"assistant-15686917-33cf-5cd0-b638-464c24c5f3bd","sessionId":"7d94da9f-3039-c913-91ee-2cdfc57aa07d","turnId":"turn-9b56c2812966de54ca2f494fe15e3ea5","inputEntryId":"user-turn-9b56c2812966de54ca2f494fe15e3ea5-1","createdAt":1794282566096,"updatedAt":1794282566096,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Fixed the caching issue** by splitting the system prompt into two separate cache blocks in `bot.py`:\n\n- **Block 1:** Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (never changes)\n- **Block 2:** Volatile `athlete_context` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language)\n\nThis ensures that when `save_fact` modifies the athlete's facts (in Block 2), only that block is invalidated in the cache, while the static instructions (Block 1) remain cached and are read at ~10% price on subsequent requests.\n\n**Created ANSWER.md** documenting the change and confirming which parts of the colleague's note applied (the two-segment cache approach, byte-stable static block, volatile tail block) and which were noted but not directly used (tool filtering considerations, rejected per-message personalization)."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
